                        "entry_id": "74b76caf-1bbb-3860-bc2e-60180ef2c0ec",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Adepte du luddisme."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "4bdd5df7-cf7f-4137-8072-d51c27812df6",
                                "sense_id": "eea4ed21-4973-3ed4-8578-360002ae7117",
                                "text": "Son auteur, professeur d’anglais, s’empresse de prouver sa bonne foi : « Je n’ai rien d’un luddiste du XXᵉ siècle se révoltant contre les machines parce qu’elles menacent l’existence de l’artisanat."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "e74e707e-b415-44f8-b362-7561d60f2d23",
                        "source_entry_id": "74b76caf-1bbb-3860-bc2e-60180ef2c0ec",
                        "source_sense_id": "eea4ed21-4973-3ed4-8578-360002ae7117",
                        "target_lang_word": "Luddite",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Luddite",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "545a87c5-3c57-3ef7-835d-ac365301b799",
                                        "entry_id": "4e412ef3-add9-31bc-a616-418473f805c4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any of a group of early-19th-century English textile workers who destroyed machinery because it would harm their livelihood."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "historical"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dd48e6d4-b550-4fbf-b7dc-29caba89d872",
                                                "sense_id": "545a87c5-3c57-3ef7-835d-ac365301b799",
                                                "text": "For instance, the Luddites, so maligned as technology-fearing machine breakers, were a highly sophisticated insurrectionary movement, composed of small, well-disciplined groups who used disguises and watchwords, raised funds and gathered arms, terrorized their opponents, and carried out well-planned, targeted attacks. (And, while it is true the Luddite movement ultimately failed, it was only after Parliament had mobilized twelve thousand troops to put it down – more troops than had fought in the Peninsular War.)"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4814ed3b-7cc9-3a5f-882a-a1af6a8f7d17",
                                        "entry_id": "4e412ef3-add9-31bc-a616-418473f805c4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Someone who opposes technological change."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "broadly",
                                            "derogatory",
                                            "often"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ddbcaf0d-29f7-4614-8e03-2b7430c629b3",
                                                "sense_id": "4814ed3b-7cc9-3a5f-882a-a1af6a8f7d17",
                                                "text": "[Benjamin Friedman] added, \"How long does it take the Luddites to be wrong — a few years, a decade, a couple of decades?\" Perhaps just as important, what happens to the workers who happen to be living during a time when the Luddite argument has some truth to it?"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "408c74d0-ade1-30c3-abfa-536784f4dd12",
                                        "entry_id": "4e412ef3-add9-31bc-a616-418473f805c4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "One who lives among nature, forsaking technology."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "broadly",
                                            "informal"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
